    "result_text": "The test suite is green. The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (2 tests), and both pass, along with a full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field \u2014 `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nThe DTOs in this project are generated from the OpenAPI spec at build time, so the change has two parts:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema (a string enum of `EMAIL`/`PHONE`), following the same pattern as the other derived fields like `displayName`, `initials`, and `bulkSignupWarning`. This generates `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` and the corresponding getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that derives the value from the owner's email:\n   ```java\n   owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.EMAIL\n       : OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum.PHONE\n   ```\n\nBecause it's computed in the mapper (the same place `displayName`/`initials` are derived), it's populated consistently for every response path \u2014 `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the create response, and list/page endpoints \u2014 with no controller changes needed.",
